      "text": "スラッシュマツ とは、マツ科マツ属の常緑高木。カリビアマツとも呼ばれる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Pinus elliottii」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinus_elliottii",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1375587202,
      "text": "Pinus elliottii, commonly known as slash pine, is a species of conifer in the family Pinaceae, a pine native to the coastal plain of the Southeastern United States. Slash pine is named after the \"slashes\" – swampy ground overgrown with trees and bushes – that constitute its habitat. Other common names include swamp pine, yellow slash pine, and southern Florida pine. Slash pine has two different varieties: P. e. var. elliottii and P. e. var. densa. Historically, slash pine has been an important economic timber for naval stores, turpentine, and resin. The wood of slash pine is known for its unusually high strength, especially for a pine. It exceeds many hardwoods and is even comparable to very dense woods such as black ironwood."
    }
